From 690f1beb394fe690f466f552d9afd6ec0c6c4877 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 04:33:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cuda/hip: the routed SwiGLU q8_1 quantize as a cross-block
 matvec epilogue (+0.6% decode)

A q8_1 block needs 32 consecutive destination elements; mul_mat_vec_q gives each
block rows_per_cuda_block of them, so the 32 live in QK8_1/rpb different blocks
and no block can quantize on its own. That is why round 37 closed both the
guest and the fold framings for this launch.

An arrival counter reaches it without a grid barrier. Each block publishes its
outputs with a device-scope fence and bumps its group counter; the block that
observes the last arrival is ordered after every other store, so it - and only
it - re-reads the group 32 floats and runs glu_quant_store. Nobody spins, and
the closing block zeroes the slot so the counters are self-clearing across a
HIP graph replay.

Bit-identical by construction: the 32 values are the exact f32 words this launch
stored, read back through memory as the separate quantize_q8_1 launch would have
read them, and glu_quant_store is that kernel arithmetic statement for
statement.

531 -> 491 dispatches/token, exactly -40. GGML_CUDA_MMVQ_Q8_1_TAIL=0 restores
the standalone launch.
